resetConnections [SimTalk]
Resets the existing connections of the PatchMatrix designated by <Path> to their predecessors and
successors, i.e. it cuts the connections.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.resetConnections
Example
Patchmatrix.resetConnections
SimTalk
setConnections [SimTalk]
See also
Connections [PatchMatrix]
resetConnections [SimTalk]
11-2962 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

setConnections [SimTalk]
Establishes the connections between the predecessors and the successors of the PatchMatrix designated
by <Path> (connect is true) or it cuts the connection (connect is false).
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.setConnections(Pred:any, Succ:any, connect:boolean) → array
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Pred of data type any designates the predecessor(s).
The parameter Pred can either be the number of the predecessor, the name of the predecessor, or an
array of predecessor numbers.
• The parameter Succ of data type any designates the successor(s).
The parameter Succ can either be the number of the successor, the name of the successor, or an array of
successor numbers.
• The parameter connect of data type boolean sets if the Pipes are going to be connected (true) or not
(false).
Example
Patchmatrix.setConnections(1,2,true)
Patchmatrix.setConnections(1,[1,2],true)
Patchmatrix.setConnections("PipeIn1","PipeOut2",false)
SimTalk
getConnectionsForPred [SimTalk]
getConnectionsForSucc [SimTalk]
resetConnections [SimTalk]
See also
Connections [PatchMatrix]
setConnections [SimTalk]
